# Gallery Photo Metadata Standard

Every entry in `_data/gallery.yml` must include **what, where, when** in the `alt` text so visitors know the context when hovering or viewing in the lightbox.

## Required Format

Each `alt` field must contain:
1. **What** — the activity or event (e.g., "Presenting", "Keynote", "Family photo")
2. **Where** — the location or event name (e.g., "AnsibleFest 2025", "Nara, Japan", "Carrboro, NC")
3. **When** — the year (included in `alt` text AND as the `year` field)

## Examples

```yaml
# ✅ GOOD — has what, where, when
- src: "/assets/images/example.png"
  alt: "Presenting at the Red Hat booth — Cisco Live 2024, Las Vegas"
  category: "booth"
  year: 2024

# ✅ GOOD — personal photo with context
- src: "/assets/images/example2.png"
  alt: "Four on the 4th race with Ivan — Carrboro, NC, 2026"
  category: "people"
  year: 2026

# ❌ BAD — missing location and year in alt
- src: "/assets/images/example3.png"
  alt: "Presenting at the Red Hat booth"
  category: "booth"
  year: 2024

# ❌ BAD — missing what happened
- src: "/assets/images/example4.png"
  alt: "Cisco Live 2024"
  category: "stage"
  year: 2024
```
